[{:db/id "q-49411/selection/d668ef8f0e0607736d65dcbcd6b198466be536a173e4879def27d489cbbe3f39" :answer/id #uuid "fe03f578-571b-540d-9ef3-181a8e51e77c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49411/selection/459c25178d54030b8b9537c5842fbabd1e7ec073782cc0e41f6207ef94c10c58" :answer/id #uuid "e3c8c753-e20b-5a57-9747-dedcf8624012" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49411/selection/339d4534539b15f6397e686d9ad8ffec1a0d391df96e7bb49f400474b3f3ab98" :answer/id #uuid "d1d532aa-8958-5aa1-b8cf-7fbdf8c1e823" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49411/selection/eb792f812701ba95f974e10e2cb665ba3e385b0d3dcb05634661e66b1f5856e6" :answer/id #uuid "95478d83-2b74-54d6-b2ce-4b4d621257a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49411/selection/08c1a79a51bb838d17cf0cf224ab340d12d8923ded0150e9c7bd9260a704d7c5" :answer/id #uuid "0dc50da8-06cb-577e-8f11-1aff146f7f81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49411/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "949bdaac-b6c0-5c99-bf9e-a00284063bb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49411/selection/08c1a79a51bb838d17cf0cf224ab340d12d8923ded0150e9c7bd9260a704d7c5" :answer-field/choices ["q-49411/selection/d668ef8f0e0607736d65dcbcd6b198466be536a173e4879def27d489cbbe3f39" "q-49411/selection/459c25178d54030b8b9537c5842fbabd1e7ec073782cc0e41f6207ef94c10c58" "q-49411/selection/339d4534539b15f6397e686d9ad8ffec1a0d391df96e7bb49f400474b3f3ab98" "q-49411/selection/eb792f812701ba95f974e10e2cb665ba3e385b0d3dcb05634661e66b1f5856e6" "q-49411/selection/08c1a79a51bb838d17cf0cf224ab340d12d8923ded0150e9c7bd9260a704d7c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49411" :question/id #uuid "8b29eab9-2700-5c7a-9162-4cf65ec05697" :question/math-academy-id "q-49411" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3x-2}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 \\\\  & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x-2}{x+1}=3-\\frac{5}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x-2}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3-\\frac{5}{x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-49411/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49411"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352220/field-1/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab" :answer/id #uuid "4a8d662c-a28d-5dfd-9f84-bd201ce8da28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352220/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c49b648-fb1f-5e74-9030-5004cd410fe7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352220/field-1/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab" :answer-field/choices ["q-352220/field-1/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352220/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "cb8bc45e-9e88-508e-9118-f6d3b447c114" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352220/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c6b66ef-9248-517c-bd70-4a8da2f2b42d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352220/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-352220/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352220" :question/id #uuid "f3bfb7fe-e8c7-55e0-8fa0-25b966f35697" :question/math-academy-id "q-352220" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{9x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $9$ | $7$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-36$ |\n|  | $9$ | $-29$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{9x+7}{x+4}=9-\\frac{29}{x+4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{9x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}(9-\\frac{29}{x+4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\text{d}x-29{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9x\\,{|}_{-1}^{2}-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|\\,{|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =9(2-(-1))-29(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-1+4|) \\\\  & =27-29(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =27-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{6}{3}) \\\\  & =27-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,2\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352220/field-1" "q-352220/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352220"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352219/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "d79c989b-6593-5652-8d35-7984dcc4d651" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352219/field-1/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "48af1386-88ba-5186-b23c-fc6da9ac5045" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352219/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "54f57a12-9bed-5b83-bc99-22e551a8f2dd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352219/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer-field/choices ["q-352219/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-352219/field-1/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352219/field-2/29648ef4e020fc43d1b46acbdbbedfd18f3de75ade3ca2e0ef505839d2f8c39b" :answer/id #uuid "a9a6fd3e-be42-5fa6-b11c-40399135f34f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352219/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2254b8e-e025-5f34-bb1b-88840799d44e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352219/field-2/29648ef4e020fc43d1b46acbdbbedfd18f3de75ade3ca2e0ef505839d2f8c39b" :answer-field/choices ["q-352219/field-2/29648ef4e020fc43d1b46acbdbbedfd18f3de75ade3ca2e0ef505839d2f8c39b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352219" :question/id #uuid "29ec841b-5e16-5ecb-8bc2-624dbc400c03" :question/math-academy-id "q-352219" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{8x+1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,23\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $8$ | $1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-24$ |\n|  | $8$ | $-23$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{8x+1}{x+3}=8-\\frac{23}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{8x+1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}(8-\\frac{23}{x+3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\text{d}x-23{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8x\\,{|}_{2}^{4}-23\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|\\,{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =8(4-2)-23(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+3|) \\\\  & =16-23(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5) \\\\  & =16-23\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{7}{5}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352219/field-1" "q-352219/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352219"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352247/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "bacdac22-7c6b-5b85-b2f1-d72f1101efe9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352247/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4889729-35b6-598a-81ae-72b11a53eaa5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352247/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-352247/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352247" :question/id #uuid "be9ad5b5-e9ad-553d-b5f1-2e80ee4b4ad4" :question/math-academy-id "q-352247" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $-7$ | $5$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $3$ | $-4$ | $1$ |\n|  | $3$ | $-4$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}=3{x}^{2}-4x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-4x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{|}_{1}^{2}-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2}+x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}{|}_{1}^{2}-2{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2}+x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[{2}^{3}-{1}^{3}]-2[{2}^{2}-{1}^{2}]+[2-1] \\\\  & =7\\cdot 1-2(3)+1 \\\\  & =7-6+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352247/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352247"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49457/selection/bd0b2d1d63a63d8fabb5ca31f42c9143215aa1d37a28c410b650acb2e335a497" :answer/id #uuid "28fcf979-ed78-5f4c-873a-9d463851fb72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49457/selection/1f5b353af7cbb90a89e4a07f196cff5b0ba27d9934d00e9a38de61eff80108f7" :answer/id #uuid "6ab2c672-ea2f-591b-a6e6-5db800760e44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49457/selection/dbf39b92e39ac3bf966fd7a477d35600eef37ac90fc4576f6dbdb99ef3fe3ea7" :answer/id #uuid "7343b116-ffdf-5ff8-bfd1-c0af3a62c4fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49457/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "d6efbcbb-0082-5883-b3ca-24de6877d7c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49457/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" :answer/id #uuid "b43ee77e-72d0-5d5f-b330-cd6323b7c326" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49457/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "90febbfa-f053-5bdc-8df9-47ca6db870a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49457/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer-field/choices ["q-49457/selection/bd0b2d1d63a63d8fabb5ca31f42c9143215aa1d37a28c410b650acb2e335a497" "q-49457/selection/1f5b353af7cbb90a89e4a07f196cff5b0ba27d9934d00e9a38de61eff80108f7" "q-49457/selection/dbf39b92e39ac3bf966fd7a477d35600eef37ac90fc4576f6dbdb99ef3fe3ea7" "q-49457/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-49457/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49457" :question/id #uuid "b1fe983d-a812-574b-a770-af40f5ba5920" :question/math-academy-id "q-49457" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{2}+7x+10}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -5 & 1 & 7 & 10 \\\\  & ↓ & -5 & -10 \\\\  & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+7x+10}{x+5}=x+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{2}+7x+10}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1}+2x{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}]+2[1-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49457/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49457"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352246/field-1/f7e0ddf094e193f19f45f558390669c9c07e6d10f3e3ead2989b7db0b6a77d28" :answer/id #uuid "7b08c6d1-b0ef-5251-8fcd-8130d4bd8ff7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{33}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352246/field-1/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" :answer/id #uuid "ba322277-f833-5b0f-b6ff-1b153f0ed981" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352246/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e8f13992-7cd8-53d4-bc5f-ebe64335c164" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352246/field-1/f7e0ddf094e193f19f45f558390669c9c07e6d10f3e3ead2989b7db0b6a77d28" :answer-field/choices ["q-352246/field-1/f7e0ddf094e193f19f45f558390669c9c07e6d10f3e3ead2989b7db0b6a77d28" "q-352246/field-1/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352246/field-2/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" :answer/id #uuid "68d838cc-4447-5437-91aa-e0933b13b858" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352246/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "08551bad-3dfc-5628-ac2b-6fb8af17a13a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352246/field-2/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" :answer-field/choices ["q-352246/field-2/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352246" :question/id #uuid "72030db9-28d9-5270-aae9-585679ac8d61" :question/math-academy-id "q-352246" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $1$ | $8$ | $7$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-4$ | $-16$ |\n|  | $1$ | $4$ | $-9$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}=x+4-\\frac{9}{x+4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x+4-\\frac{9}{x+4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}x-9{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{3}+4x\\,{|}_{0}^{3}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|\\,{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{2}-{0}^{2})+4(3-0)-9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3+4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+4|) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}+12-9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{2}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{7}{4}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352246/field-1" "q-352246/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352246"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49460/selection/853c52485635d05d40d03c3aaa9bc790950960d020345e87e8d39338a34b6c10" :answer/id #uuid "c52c9408-bf3d-53ad-bc0c-046483dd7202" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-6x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49460/selection/d43f01fe26b518b27a2de3bd8aac9964faf2d5d74294620c8ba3643dda26d8ea" :answer/id #uuid "25fa8cc0-437f-50fe-927a-666aef4fbdcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49460/selection/5c2fb971f094500c8c1ff4d0862c2a2bdb2e04a388ca957e5f8f9cefe7da090e" :answer/id #uuid "1ba17ce9-7b82-5167-9964-a423e881e326" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49460/selection/af51b8d5e82348d3a7b0ad96115ad801abb9238edcefa670441dee364f9a47f1" :answer/id #uuid "e778c959-be05-5546-be89-1b654eef9bc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+3x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49460/selection/57fba23103d3414d4781f5db494933888ad0d7cf7a08ea44949524fca8e52e20" :answer/id #uuid "98ab4987-2a41-5a6d-83a7-c8c16687755d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}x-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49460/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9f45fc8-1d4f-501e-bd8a-601eea9dbece" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49460/selection/af51b8d5e82348d3a7b0ad96115ad801abb9238edcefa670441dee364f9a47f1" :answer-field/choices ["q-49460/selection/853c52485635d05d40d03c3aaa9bc790950960d020345e87e8d39338a34b6c10" "q-49460/selection/d43f01fe26b518b27a2de3bd8aac9964faf2d5d74294620c8ba3643dda26d8ea" "q-49460/selection/5c2fb971f094500c8c1ff4d0862c2a2bdb2e04a388ca957e5f8f9cefe7da090e" "q-49460/selection/af51b8d5e82348d3a7b0ad96115ad801abb9238edcefa670441dee364f9a47f1" "q-49460/selection/57fba23103d3414d4781f5db494933888ad0d7cf7a08ea44949524fca8e52e20"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49460" :question/id #uuid "910ac292-9317-5cd0-9e18-28f3dc011864" :question/math-academy-id "q-49460" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-6}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & 3 & -6 \\\\  & ↓ & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\  & 1 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-6}{x-2}={x}^{2}+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-6}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}+3)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+3x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-49460/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49460"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49357/selection/669758227e9695b09dd2a960f0716901cc151600b6d6a13dd526ecee976f9961" :answer/id #uuid "ea9e3dbe-b937-58b8-9363-fd41269fe2cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49357/selection/059a34e3d2dd1959b09e4d0f0516d898ad8a60a7c9a5cbeb3e7e9f79814b276b" :answer/id #uuid "0ac7904f-19ce-541b-9ac3-bd28f600e25b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{3}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49357/selection/a692537d703a7591d61f1f359800fdd45743cb1aff7715d43777875bcf1b0101" :answer/id #uuid "738bfa19-a25e-5250-94a7-2d2484b36938" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49357/selection/a506ee10f84ed465892caaed66eb1845b6748babaf4bcac844a872702245a08d" :answer/id #uuid "972880a6-8ea1-5a69-9541-a50a262281d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49357/selection/41aac3fa6d96f3756eb9bba27d31481537ce6260e88b4876aa57b6f24644d52c" :answer/id #uuid "a991d633-29cf-517b-b6a6-d56774d2ab3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49357/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d86b8f94-f6d0-53df-a9e6-f2d867878db1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49357/selection/059a34e3d2dd1959b09e4d0f0516d898ad8a60a7c9a5cbeb3e7e9f79814b276b" :answer-field/choices ["q-49357/selection/669758227e9695b09dd2a960f0716901cc151600b6d6a13dd526ecee976f9961" "q-49357/selection/059a34e3d2dd1959b09e4d0f0516d898ad8a60a7c9a5cbeb3e7e9f79814b276b" "q-49357/selection/a692537d703a7591d61f1f359800fdd45743cb1aff7715d43777875bcf1b0101" "q-49357/selection/a506ee10f84ed465892caaed66eb1845b6748babaf4bcac844a872702245a08d" "q-49357/selection/41aac3fa6d96f3756eb9bba27d31481537ce6260e88b4876aa57b6f24644d52c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49357" :question/id #uuid "9156045e-7fa2-5298-b62c-0937c4d32fb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-49357" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{x+1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $4$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x+1}{4(x+\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4} & 1 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & 1 & \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{4})} & =1+\\frac{(\\frac{3}{4})}{(x+\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{3}{4(x+\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{3}{4x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int (1+\\frac{3}{4x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\int \\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[x+\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{3}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49357/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49357"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73390/selection/6deb1078ff6edea399c9293b4fe14902878addafe1a61b881441cba741159d33" :answer/id #uuid "26c59c69-aef0-5756-a801-b22197849d24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73390/selection/d23d631ca61a8cc5e7fee8d14059705e597e58c73e5a33bf0a6f8f430f611c31" :answer/id #uuid "dd051e7f-653f-553d-8e8a-9cae7e72c20e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73390/selection/2e4a9a1d1a1aa47f315562a48f22cd436daa1e3a0225ac66942c4eb5231613d5" :answer/id #uuid "2b60b452-aacd-56fd-b7af-9b124c7c01d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73390/selection/4240ba5ab793d32dbb68a10149445c1896c4002800ebdfcde33c2d2e74d29a3e" :answer/id #uuid "fd4d0715-faea-5b22-87f5-e07729136917" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73390/selection/edf4461b5e6d646e70c5e876a4030a10babd1f703757162ca8ba30ba8a679ea0" :answer/id #uuid "986b5070-d35a-5a1f-b8fb-7d0830d61f54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73390/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "11558995-4bba-5309-bf1c-92b647e9d322" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73390/selection/4240ba5ab793d32dbb68a10149445c1896c4002800ebdfcde33c2d2e74d29a3e" :answer-field/choices ["q-73390/selection/6deb1078ff6edea399c9293b4fe14902878addafe1a61b881441cba741159d33" "q-73390/selection/d23d631ca61a8cc5e7fee8d14059705e597e58c73e5a33bf0a6f8f430f611c31" "q-73390/selection/2e4a9a1d1a1aa47f315562a48f22cd436daa1e3a0225ac66942c4eb5231613d5" "q-73390/selection/4240ba5ab793d32dbb68a10149445c1896c4002800ebdfcde33c2d2e74d29a3e" "q-73390/selection/edf4461b5e6d646e70c5e876a4030a10babd1f703757162ca8ba30ba8a679ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73390" :question/id #uuid "33ca9b7c-fc9e-559a-a429-545cdd28eedd" :question/math-academy-id "q-73390" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{8x-1}{4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $4$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8x-1}{4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8x-1}{4(x-\\frac{3}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{8x-1}{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & 8 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & 6 \\\\  & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x-1}{(x-\\frac{3}{4})} & =8+\\frac{5}{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8x-1}{4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int (8+\\frac{5}{x-\\frac{3}{4}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8\\int \\text{d}x+5\\int \\frac{1}{x-\\frac{3}{4}}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|]+C \\\\  & =2x+\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73390/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73390"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-358987/field-1/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "9e011deb-b0b4-5fd4-8afe-862e648f4515" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-358987/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "f24a8ed1-7d98-5485-a8ea-4103a4484b38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-358987/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "95589281-5b67-5528-afdb-baf9b389e061" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-358987/field-1/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer-field/choices ["q-358987/field-1/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" "q-358987/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-358987/field-2/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "69df8fcc-df88-5ffc-a68d-6b44fd7cf15b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-358987/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "300819cd-134b-5280-af9f-cd770314968c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-358987/field-2/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-358987/field-2/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-358987" :question/id #uuid "b6597e0e-678e-53cf-896b-1b7f4502efe0" :question/math-academy-id "q-358987" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{7}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $3$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3(x-2/3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{(x-2/3)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $4$ | $-5$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $\\frac{8}{3}$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-\\frac{7}{3}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x-5}{(x-2/3)} & =4-\\frac{(7/3)}{(x-2/3)} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{7}{3x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(4-\\frac{7}{3x-2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[4{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\text{d}x-7{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[4x-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[4(3-1)-\\frac{7}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[8-\\frac{7\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{7}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-358987/field-1" "q-358987/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-358987"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-358835/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "c25042b5-238c-561d-a835-d11002ded149" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-358835/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "744ab197-f2d4-5274-8f96-087886feaa13" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-358835/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer-field/choices ["q-358835/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-358835/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "e4ec6380-bbae-5d10-ab99-fe55633b30a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-358835/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2085e0d5-c4db-58ea-a66f-f821d9ef6442" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-358835/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-358835/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-358835" :question/id #uuid "22bd6b2f-502e-5ce3-99ef-deb51dae08a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-358835" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-3}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{11}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-3}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-3}{2(x+1/2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-3}{(x+1/2)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $5$ | $-3$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-\\frac{5}{2}$ |\n|  | $5$ | $-\\frac{11}{2}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-3}{(x+1/2)} & =5-\\frac{(11/2)}{(x+1/2)} \\\\  & =5-\\frac{11}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-3}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(5-\\frac{11}{2x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x-11{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[5x-\\frac{11}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5(1-0)-\\frac{11}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5-\\frac{11\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{11}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-358835/field-1" "q-358835/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-358835"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114896/selection/11bea3563c00de94024aa45d93d33db704bd97f2446b57b9f6ef42bfe8e7d559" :answer/id #uuid "dc457955-dab3-5ba4-8f77-192fa422c9b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114896/selection/3d7d7aadd1e7887dfe7c32c746707910757ff373f924a04e9f44faacb79db6a5" :answer/id #uuid "888ad65f-a721-54b1-b41c-34e3bc0c23f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}(1+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114896/selection/2aec4bf042fbdcfd61811ce52a52a71269aa0d9df188d53db4386754da5caaec" :answer/id #uuid "bb9339b1-122b-59d1-8567-006b41ab76e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}(3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114896/selection/b020557689a2afc740b82397b5461ffe6879e8b9e531ea13678913ff3a764b03" :answer/id #uuid "e54e893f-8cf1-5283-9bd0-cea00ff72973" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114896/selection/9276cad3e5bab92f9f3fa107d488488bad38701d12c1362b61f163ad3f0a7fea" :answer/id #uuid "cc4ec236-5e1b-5724-97ef-8409b74f976c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}(5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114896/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "edbb6eef-4442-5b15-8560-cfa9b2fce45e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114896/selection/b020557689a2afc740b82397b5461ffe6879e8b9e531ea13678913ff3a764b03" :answer-field/choices ["q-114896/selection/11bea3563c00de94024aa45d93d33db704bd97f2446b57b9f6ef42bfe8e7d559" "q-114896/selection/3d7d7aadd1e7887dfe7c32c746707910757ff373f924a04e9f44faacb79db6a5" "q-114896/selection/2aec4bf042fbdcfd61811ce52a52a71269aa0d9df188d53db4386754da5caaec" "q-114896/selection/b020557689a2afc740b82397b5461ffe6879e8b9e531ea13678913ff3a764b03" "q-114896/selection/9276cad3e5bab92f9f3fa107d488488bad38701d12c1362b61f163ad3f0a7fea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114896" :question/id #uuid "9cb05493-3a43-5cd7-9456-a6491428f397" :question/math-academy-id "q-114896" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $6$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6(x+\\frac{1}{6})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & 2 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & 2 & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})} & =2+\\frac{(\\frac{2}{3})}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{4}{6x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}(2+\\frac{4}{6x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[2x+\\frac{4}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+1|]}_{-1/12}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[2x+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+1|]}_{-1/12}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2(0-(-\\frac{1}{12}))+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6(0)+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6(-\\frac{1}{12})+1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2(\\frac{1}{12})+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-114896/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114896"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
